@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# The declared consumer down-projection inventory (gmeow:ProjectionProfile) — one
# row per authored dsl/mappings/projections/*.ttl document, with the raise-only
# floor on the number of gmeow:ProjectionMapping cells that document must declare.
#
# The gate (crates/pipeline/src/projection_profiles.rs) requires the declared path
# set to EQUAL the on-disk set in both directions and every profile's authored cell
# count to hold at or above its floor. A deleted profile, an unregistered new one,
# and a profile hollowed out to fewer cells are all hard failures — none of which
# any generated-artifact inventory could see, because several profiles bind the
# same gmeow:profile name and therefore share one generated query and one EDOAL
# alignment.
#
# Floors RISE with the surface and never fall. Retiring a consumer surface deletes
# the whole row together with the document it names.

gmeow:projProfile-ai a gmeow:ProjectionProfile ;
    rdfs:label "projection profile — AI / model cards"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:profileSource "dsl/mappings/projections/ai.ttl" ;
    gmeow:profileCellMinimum 4 .

